---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Matt Rabah is a Detroit-based CX, customer success, and implementation professional focused on customer lifecycle systems, CRM discipline, and practical AI workflows."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>

    <h1 class="display">I build the operating layer customers feel.</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      My work sits between CX, customer success, implementation, and CRM
      discipline, with practical AI layered in where it earns its place.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="background">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="background">Background</h2>
    </header>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I have spent seven-plus years across NeuroSync, Shinola, and Context By
      Design. The thread across that work is simple: customers feel the
      operating model. They feel the handoff, the missed note, the unclear
      owner, the delayed follow-up, and the moment a team has to rediscover what
      should already be known.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I have worked across healthcare accounts, high-touch client experience,
      portfolio growth, Salesforce process, lifecycle diagnostics, onboarding,
      retention systems, and executive-facing account work. Different
      industries, same underlying problem: customer experience breaks when
      ownership is vague.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I hold an M.S. in Customer Experience Management from Michigan State
      University's Eli Broad College of Business and a B.S. in Organizational
      Behavior from Oakland University. I am a Salesforce Certified Platform
      Administrator, with additional certifications in business intelligence and
      inbound marketing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="focus">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="focus">Current focus</h2>
    </header>

    <p class="about-prose">
      My current focus is practical AI in customer-facing operations. Not AI as
      a novelty layer, but AI as a way to reduce administrative drag, prepare
      better, surface risk earlier, and help teams make cleaner decisions
      without blurring accountability.
    </p>

    <p class="about-prose">
      Healthtech, medtech, and other regulated environments are strong fits,
      because trust is fragile there and implementation discipline matters. But
      the broader work is the same everywhere: customer lifecycle design for
      complex teams. Clear owners, usable systems, better handoffs, and fewer
      surprises near renewal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="next">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="next">Let's talk</h2>
      <a href="/contact" class="section-more">Contact →</a>
    </header>

    <p class="about-prose">
      I am currently open to roles in customer success, CX, implementation, and
      RevOps-adjacent work. If that is what you are hiring for, I would like to
      hear about it.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
